Mindworx Compliance Agent – Process Map & Agent Specification
Executive Summary
The Mindworx Compliance Agent (working name: ComplianceOS) turns the Academy's compliance and QAC procedures into automated, gate-driven checks so that recurring mistakes stop reaching SETA, QCTO and EISA evaluators. Compliance and quality assurance are the part of the Academy where errors recur most, so every procedure Phyllis Muthombeni mapped on 14 October 2026 becomes a check the agent runs.
The agent works on four pillars: QCTO registration, monitoring and EISA readiness; MICT SETA registration, verification and accreditation; document QA (assessor and moderator scope, PoEs, SoRs, SLAs); and B-BBEE skills development evidence. Nothing is submitted to MICT SETA or QCTO, and no EISA exam goes ahead, until the agent has cleared the matching gate.
The agent has three jobs: check documents as they arrive, track expiry dates before they lapse, and compile complete audit files before each site visit. It prepares every file and submits applications to MICT SETA and QCTO once the Compliance Officer approves them.
Detailed Automated Gate Functions
Nine gates cover every procedure walked through on 14 October; each has a validation rule and a system action.
1. Onboarding Gate
* Automated validation: Picks the agreement set by learner type (employed, unemployed, bank). Scans certified IDs, qualifications and CVs for legibility, a certification stamp and a certification date within the last 3 months. Non-South Africans need a certified passport.
* System action: Blocks SETA and QCTO registration until every file is verified. Sends the learner a list of what is missing.
2. Registration Gate
* Automated validation: Builds the MICT SETA bulk upload file and the QCTO enrolment forms from verified records only.
* System action: Tracks each learner until the SETA Proof of Registration arrives. Starts the QCTO monitoring countdown on the registration date.
3. Assessor & Moderator Scope Gate
* Automated validation: Checks registration numbers, qualification scope and expiry dates against the delivery calendar. Confirms a signed SLA with Mindworx.
* System action: Alerts 90 days before expiry. Blocks an expired assessor or moderator from signing PoEs or moderation samples.
4. QCTO Monitoring Visit Gate
QCTO visits between 21 days and 2 months after registration to confirm the learnership is being implemented. The agent compiles the file below and flags gaps two weeks before the window opens.
* Assessor accreditation, certified IDs or passports, CVs and certified qualifications
* SDP accreditation letter and SDP standard operating procedures
* Training schedule, assessment strategy, timetables and lesson plans
* QCTO registration letters for the learners
* Facility check: furniture, lighting, cleanliness and ventilation (or proof of the online delivery method)
* Minutes of meetings, learnership agreements, certified learner IDs and onboarding induction report
5. Verification Gate (on course completion)
* Trigger: Assessor and moderation reports arrive.
* Automated validation: Drafts the Statement of Results (SoR) and completion letters. Compiles the verification file: assessor and moderator reports, their SETA registration letters, SLA with Mindworx, SDP accreditation letter, learner transcripts, SoR sheet and learner PoEs.
* System action: Blocks the MICT SETA application until the file is complete, then submits it once approved. Confirms a moderator is booked for the verification site visit. Logs the signed verification report and tracks certificates until received.
6. Post-Course Review Gate
* Automated validation: Confirms SoRs, client reference letters, and completed knowledge, practical and workplace module PoEs.
* System action: Marks the cohort ready for EISA only when every learner's modules are complete.
7. EISA Exam Readiness Gate
* Automated validation: Scores the venue and staffing checklist:
   * Venue: laptops, screens, learner name tags, table numbers, seating plan, signage to the exam centre and bathrooms
   * Documents: valid accreditation letter, wall clock, registers, site report and video report
   * Staff: 2 invigilators per room, 1 chief invigilator, training manager, IT support, staff name tags
* System action: Flags CRITICAL NON-COMPLIANCE if invigilator ratios, accreditation or equipment are incomplete.
8. New Qualification Accreditation Gate (any time)
* Automated validation: Compiles the SETA/QCTO accreditation pack: facilitator documents and accreditation letters, valid company stamp, lease agreement, tax compliance status, public liability insurance, SLAs, staff IDs and qualifications, OHS representative appointment, first aid kit, venue evidence and proof of online training method.
* System action: Shows a readiness score per document and blocks submission until all are current.
9. B-BBEE Evidence Gate
* Automated validation: Assembles signed agreements, verified IDs, disability certificates where claimed, stipend proof and payslips, SETA registration letters, SoRs and absorption letters.
* System action: Reconciles trained seats with WSP/ATR submissions before the cohort closes, and feeds the client B-BBEE self-service portal.
